    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For the in-text citation in APA 7th edition, you'll generally list the first author followed by \"et al.\" for the first citation, and then for subsequent citations, you'll use the same format. In the Chicago style (Notes and Bibliography), you typically use a footnote or endnote with the full citation the first time, and then a shortened version in subsequent notes. For author-date Chicago, it's similar to APA, using the author's last name and year.\n\nIt's crucial to check your specific style guide requirements, as there can be subtle variations, especially depending on whether you are using Notes-Bibliography or Author-Date Chicago. Remember, consistency is key in your literature review, so pick a format and stick to it!",
